==English==
{{was wotd|2018|November|26}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|illūstris||bright, shining; distinguished, prominent, illustrious}} {{suffix|en||ous|t2=''suffix forming adjectives from nouns, to denote possession or presence of a quality in any degree''}}. ''Illūstris'' is derived from {{m|la|illūstrō||to brighten, illuminate; to make famous or illustrious}}, from {{m|la|in-||''prefix meaning ‘in, inside’''}} + {{m|la|lustrō||to purify by making a sacrifice; to brighten, illuminate}} (from {{m|la|lustrō||purificatory sacrifice}}, possibly ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*lewk-||bright; to shine}} or {{m|ine-pro|*lewh₃-||to wash}}).

